<task id="147" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>C10 part 2 (client) — children created or re-parented in the browser through Xrm.WebApi (wizards, Notepad memos, To Do widgets, document upload, regarding resolvers) end up secure when their parent is: inventory every client writer, decide per writer (route through the BFF per WP-3, or create-then-server-fix-up per WP-5), and turn on the scheduled reconciliation as the safety net for every write outside the product</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-30, session 27; defect C10 half 2, owner round 2 item 6 "client-created children")</phase>
    <gate>after 144, 145, 146, 148 and 149 are merged. Coordinate with field-mapping-server-write-path-r1 (W3/W4/W5) before building any BFF create endpoint.</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Security-boundary change spanning client (.ts/.tsx) and BFF (.cs) write paths; tags bff-api, auth, security, frontend; enables a scheduled job that writes ownership.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Per-writer architectural decision (WP-3 vs WP-5) across ~15 client writers in five packages and a sibling project's pipeline; a wrong call leaves a disclosure window on a secure record's children.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches shared client packages (Spaarke.UI.Components wizards, SmartTodo, DailyBriefing, AI.Widgets, Notepad, EventDetailSidePane, RegardingResolver PCF) and the job/engine from 148; overlaps field-mapping-server-write-path-r1's wizard migration.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>144, 145, 146, 148, 149</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, dataverse, frontend, react, typescript, pcf, job, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>14-20 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Session 27 C10 research gap 2: "Client Xrm.WebApi creates (wizards, Notepad memos) are user-owned, and no fix-up channel exists." Owner round 2 item 6.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Many children are created in the browser, as the user, through Xrm.WebApi — Dataverse makes the creating user the owner, in the user's own business unit, so a to-do, event, memo, document or analysis created on a secure project is readable by everyone with ordinary depth in that user's BU. Inventory every client writer that creates or re-parents a child record, make each one end up with the owner and shares task 146 and task 149 define for its parent, and switch on the scheduled reconciliation (task 148's engine) so writes made outside the product — MDA forms, quick create, grid edits, imports, flows — are corrected too.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE full-stack developer (React/TypeScript shared components + BFF .NET Minimal API) on the ADR-002 server-side write path. Fail closed (ADR-003); client code previews, the server enforces (WP-2).</role>

  <goal>Every client writer in the census below produces a child that, when its parent is secure, is owned by task 144's named Secure team with shares mirrored from the parent — either because the create/re-parent now goes through a BFF path that applies the task-146 owner rule inline (WP-3), or because the client create is followed by a server fix-up call and the gap is within an owner-accepted bound (WP-5) — and task 148's reconciliation job runs on a schedule with writes enabled as the L4 safety net for every non-product write; each writer's decision and evidence are recorded.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>WHY THE CLIENT PATH LEAKS. A `Xrm.WebApi.createRecord` runs as the user: `ownerid` = the user, `owningbusinessunit` = the user's BU. Task 146 only changes BFF writers. So after 146 a to-do created through the To Do wizard on a secure project is still owned by its creator in an ordinary BU and readable by anyone there with Local/Deep Read — the same C10 exposure, through the front door. DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md §4.3 (`:109-113`) lists the client-only create paths and says the migration is "typed BFF create endpoints per invariant-bearing table … then switch each wizard's create call to the BFF"; §3 (`:72-76`) defines the L3 async fix-up (WP-5, change channel — does not exist yet) and the L4 scheduled reconciliation (ADR-036).

CLIENT WRITER CENSUS (verified 2026-09-30 by grep of `createRecord('sprk_…')` / `updateRecord` over src/client and src/solutions; the executor re-runs it and adds anything new, including raw `fetch` POSTs to `/api/data/` and PCF sources whose built bundles matched):
  CREATE
  • `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateTodoWizard/todoService.ts:281` (sprk_todo)
  • `.../CreateEventWizard/eventService.ts:411` (sprk_event)
  • `.../CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/workAssignmentService.ts:671` (follow-on sprk_event; the work assignment itself is a ROOT — task 144)
  • `.../CreateInvoiceWizard/invoiceService.ts:297` (sprk_invoice)
  • `.../CreateReportCardWizard/reportCardService.ts:255` (sprk_reportcard — a child of project/matter per design.md §5.1d)
  • `src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/CreateAnalysisWizardWidget.tsx:918` (sprk_analysis) and its chained communication (`:955` target sprk_communication)
  • `src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/hooks/useInlineTodoCreate.ts:318` (sprk_todo)
  • `src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/widgets/SmartTodoWidget/SmartTodoWidget.tsx:806`, `src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/components/SmartToDo.tsx:760`, `src/solutions/SmartTodo/src/services/DataverseService.ts:506`, `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/services/DataverseService.ts:521` (sprk_todo)
  • `src/solutions/Notepad/src/hooks/useSprkMemoRepository.ts:446` (sprk_memo — parents: matter, project, event, invoice, budget, work assignment per SUPPORTED_MEMO_PARENTS)
  • `src/solutions/EventDetailSidePane/src/App.tsx:623` (sprk_memo), `:672` (sprk_todo)
  • `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/EntityCreationService.ts:752`, `.../services/document-upload/DocumentRecordService.ts:200`, `:261` (sprk_document)
  RE-PARENT (a child moved under or out of a secure parent must change owner too)
  • `src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver/RegardingResolver/handlers/ResolverWriteHandler.ts:412`, `:532` (updateRecord on the host child)
  • `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/logic/connections/ConnectionsWriteHandler.ts:244`, `:301`, `:357`, `:379` (communication regarding updates)
  NON-PRODUCT WRITES (no code to change — OOB MDA forms, quick create, editable grids, Excel/Data Import, customer flows): only a server-side fix-up or reconciliation can reach them (WP-5).

TWO GAPS INSIDE THE CENSUS THAT THE OWNER RULE EXPOSES.
  (1) `sprk_memo` is in NEITHER FR-26 taxonomy set (`src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolver.cs:56-82`, mirrored in `@spaarke/ui-components`, parity-pinned by `CoreAncestorResolverTests`), so a memo regarding an EVENT carries no stamp naming the event's project. The task-146 rule derives a child's securability from its parent lookups and stamps; for a memo on an event on a secure project it must reach the project through the event. The reconciler (148) walks that hop; the client path must too.
  (2) `sprk_document` and `sprk_invoice` carry no `sprk_regarding{core}` columns at all (phase3-backfill-runbook.md §1b), so a to-do or memo regarding a document/invoice is secure only if the document's/invoice's own parent is.

THE SIBLING PROJECT. field-mapping-server-write-path-r1 (worktree `spaarke-wt-field-mapping-server-write-path-r1`, design only as of 2026-09-30) plans W3 "typed BFF create endpoints + wizard migration" for the 8 wizards, W4 for the other product creates (Daily Briefing inline To Do, Communication, Notepad memo, EventDetailSidePane), and W5 the change-signal fix-up channel; its design §9 names UAC-r2 as owner of I-2 and says "the pipeline must leave a slot for it". This task must not fork that pipeline (CLAUDE.md §11), and must not leave a writer unfixed waiting for it (owner: nothing deferred).</background>
