  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-002 WP-2/WP-3/WP-5">Scope: every writer in the census. The client never decides or sets the owner and never shares a child itself — the server applies the task-146 owner rule and task-149 share rule (WP-2: the client may only preview). Per writer choose, in this order of preference: (A) the create/re-parent goes through a BFF path that applies the rule inline (WP-3); (B) only if (A) is impossible for that writer: the client create is immediately followed by a BFF fix-up call for that one row, with the scheduled reconciliation as backstop (WP-5). Record the choice and the reason for every writer. No writer is left on (C) "reconciliation only" without an owner decision (escalation).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11 / coordination">Scope: BFF create endpoints. Before building any typed create endpoint, check field-mapping-server-write-path-r1's state and message that session. If its W3/W4 endpoint for the table exists on master, route the writer through it and add the I-2 owner/share step into its pipeline slot; if not, build ONLY what this writer needs, in the location and shape that project's design names (`RecordCreationService` pipeline), and tell them. Never two create endpoints for one table.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every changed writer. If the server cannot resolve the owner (task 146 refusal), the user sees the server's message and the record is NOT left user-owned: under (A) nothing is created; under (B) the fix-up failure is surfaced to the user and the row is picked up by the reconciliation run. The reconciliation job never silently skips a secure-parent child it could not fix — it reports it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2">Scope: required use cases. A document-only save with no related record keeps working unchanged (no parent → no secure derivation). Nothing here makes a target record required. Existing wizard UX (steps, validation, field-mapping preview) is unchanged except where a server error must now be shown.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036 / ADR-052">Scope: the L4 safety net. Reuse task 148's `SecureChildReconciliationJob` — schedule it and enable writes in the deployed configuration; also give it a "recently modified children" pass (modifiedon watermark over the census tables) so non-product writes are corrected within one interval, not only at the next full sweep. No hand-rolled BackgroundService; no new job class for the same invariant. The interval is recorded in the note and put to the owner (escalation).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the taxonomy change. Adding `sprk_memo` to the CHILD set is made on BOTH the C# and TypeScript sides in the same change; the cross-language parity test stays green; `scripts/Backfill-CoreAncestorStamps.ps1` is run in dry-run to report memos needing a stamp, and applied in dev under the manual gate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-1 / ADR-002">Scope: all enforcement. No Dataverse plugin. No Dataverse in CI; live verification is a MANUAL gate with existing non-admin test users in their current BU; never propose relocating users.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: any new BFF route. Delegated caller auth with an explicit per-record authorization filter on the PARENT (the caller must be able to append to it), no new `.WithClientSecret(...)`; route added to RouteAuthorizationGuardTests as gated.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration or ctor null-check tests. Server fix-up paths get integration tests under `tests/integration/data-mutation/**`; client writers keep/extend their existing jest tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement decision citing bff-extensions.md for every new route; publish-size delta vs a fresh master build (short path, Compress-Archive, both sizes, file counts), ≤60 MB; CVE scan. PCF version bump in all four locations for any PCF changed (PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md); `npm run build:prod`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2">Scope: deliverable. 100% of the census writers are decided and fixed here; writers found during execution are added, not deferred.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2 item 11 / task 145 (added by review 2026-09-30)">Scope: the Secure Record Owner role's privileges. Every table a census writer creates or re-parents (at least sprk_todo, sprk_event, sprk_memo, sprk_document, sprk_invoice, sprk_reportcard, sprk_analysis, sprk_communication) must be in the ONE codified set (word-add-in-r1 task 082's JSON file, extended through task 145's procedure) and granted live before its writer ships; a missing table is added in this task through 145's script, never by widening a role by hand.</constraint>
  </constraints>

