  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL. Confirm 144/145/146/148/149 merged. Message the field-mapping-server-write-path-r1 session: ask which W3/W4 endpoints exist and when.</step>
    <step order="1">Re-run the client census (createRecord/updateRecord/raw Web API POST/PATCH of child tables and of their parent lookups, in src/client and src/solutions, including PCF sources); record every writer with file:line and which parents it can name.</step>
    <step order="2">Add `sprk_memo` to the CHILD taxonomy on both sides (parity test green); run the ancestor-stamp backfill dry run for memos and record it.</step>
    <step order="3">Decide per writer: (A) BFF path — reuse the sibling's endpoint if on master, else build the minimal one in the sibling's named shape; (B) client create + immediate BFF fix-up of that row. Record the decision table with reasons.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement each writer's change; show the server's refusal message in the UI where a create/re-parent is refused.</step>
    <step order="5">Extend task 148's job with the modifiedon-watermark pass over the census tables and a single-row fix-up entry point; schedule it and set writes enabled in the deployed configuration template; record the interval.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests: per writer, a secure-parent create ends secure-team-owned with mirrored shares (server integration for A and for the fix-up in B; client jest for the call switch); refusal leaves no user-owned row (A) or is reported and later fixed (B); a non-product write (simulated user-owned child under a secure parent) is corrected by the job's watermark pass; unfiled document save unchanged.</step>
    <step order="7">Update DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md §4.3 and the I-2 row. Build (BFF, `npm run build:prod` per package), tests, ArchTests, publish size, CVE, PCF version bumps.</step>
    <step order="8" mode="prescriptive">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev, after deploy of BFF and clients): as an existing non-admin test user shared on a secure project, a secure matter and a secure work assignment, create through each client writer (and re-parent through RegardingResolver and Connections); record owner read-back and child shares; confirm a non-sharee test user cannot open each; create one child with the OOB MDA quick-create under a secure project and record the job correcting it within the interval; delete probes and record the deletion.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md (`✅ [done]`) and the POML status; write the task note with the census and decision table.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Any writer can be fixed only by option (B) or by the reconciliation alone: the child exists user-owned in the user's BU for the fix-up latency (B) or up to one job interval (reconciliation). State the window per writer and get the owner's acceptance (CLAUDE.md §6) before shipping it; the alternative to present is routing that writer through the BFF.</trigger>
    <trigger>field-mapping-server-write-path-r1 is building the same table's create endpoint concurrently, or its pipeline cannot host the I-2 step: STOP and agree ownership of the endpoint with that project and the owner rather than building a second one.</trigger>
    <trigger>Routing a wizard create through the BFF changes `createdby` to the application user (app-only create) and a surface depends on `createdby` = the human (e.g. Daily Briefing / notifications use Created By, owner round 2 item 9; task 152 counts Created By only for human systemusers): surface the conflict (§6.5 path A/B/C) — do not silently lose the creator. The alternative, an OBO (delegated) BFF create that sets `ownerid` to the Secure team, requires the caller's role to hold `prvAssign` on that table; if it does not, do not widen user roles — present both options with the recommendation.</trigger>
    <trigger>Writes made OUTSIDE the product (OOB MDA forms, quick create, editable grids, imports, flows) can only be corrected by the reconciliation job, so each such child is user-owned in the creator's BU for up to one job interval. Put the interval (and the per-table exposure it implies) to the owner for explicit acceptance before enabling the schedule as the only control for those paths; the alternative to present is removing Create on the child tables from the MDA for secure parents (form/ribbon rules) — recorded, not silently chosen.</trigger>
    <trigger>The owner-accepted reconciliation interval cannot be met by an in-BFF ADR-036 job (load, lease, or Dataverse throttling): present the ADR-052 placement alternatives rather than shortening it unsafely.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Client writers create children only through `Xrm.WebApi`/`IDataService` (census above); `bffDataServiceAdapter` create/update target routes that do not exist (field-mapping-r1 design §2.3); no BFF path applies I-2 to a client-created row (grep `sprk_issecure` in src/client → reads only; grep `ResolveOwningTeamAsync` → no client-facing caller before task 146). Task 148's `SecureChildReconciler`/`SecureChildReconciliationJob` is the engine and trigger this task reuses.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for the fix-up and safety net: extend task 148's engine (single-row entry) and job (watermark pass) rather than adding a second job. New BFF create routes are added only where option (A) is chosen AND the sibling project has not built the endpoint, in the sibling's `RecordCreationService` shape — each one listed in the task note with its three-question justification at the time it is built.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>After task 146, every to-do, event, memo, document, invoice, report card and analysis created in the browser on a secure project, matter or work assignment is still owned by its creator in an ordinary business unit and readable in MDA by that BU at ordinary depth; and anything created through an OOB form, import or flow is never corrected.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

