  </outputs>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="To Do wizard on a secure project">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_project&amp;id={secure-project-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Sign in as an existing non-admin test user shared on the secure project.</step>
        <step>Create a To Do through the Create To Do wizard.</step>
        <step>Check the console for JavaScript errors.</step>
        <step>Open the new To Do's record and confirm Owner = the named Secure owner team.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The wizard completes as before; the record is owned by the named Secure owner team; no console errors.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Notepad memo on an event under a secure project">
      <steps>
        <step>Open an event regarding a secure project; open Notepad; create a memo.</step>
        <step>Confirm the memo's Owner = the named Secure owner team.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Memo saved and secure-team-owned; no console errors.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Server refusal is shown, not swallowed">
      <steps>
        <step>With the owner resolution forced to refuse (e.g. a secure parent that is flagged but not provisioned in a test environment), attempt a create from a wizard.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The wizard shows the server's message using the existing Fluent v9 MessageBar error pattern of that wizard; no record is left owned by the user (option A) or the job report lists it (option B).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Toggle dark mode; repeat the refusal test.</step>
        <step>Verify the error message uses Fluent v9 semantic tokens (no hard-coded colours).</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Error rendering adapts to dark mode.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The task note lists every client create/re-parent writer of a child table found by the census (file:line) with its decision (A or B) and reason; none is undecided.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a secure project, matter or work assignment, a child created through each census writer ends owned by the named Secure team and its sharees' access equals the parent's under task 149's recorded mechanism (BFF mirror asserted in the server integration test for each A route and for the B fix-up; platform cascade asserted in the manual live gate).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A child re-parented under a secure parent through RegardingResolver or Connections becomes secure-team-owned with the parent's sharee access (task 149 mechanism); one re-parented out of every secure parent returns to its new parent's BU default team and loses the mirrored shares.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE / AUTHORIZATION: no client code sets `ownerid` or writes a share on a child (grep of the changed packages for `ownerid@odata.bind` / share calls on child tables returns no new hit); a caller who cannot append to the parent cannot create or re-parent a child under it through any new route or fix-up call (fix-up refuses to act for a row the caller could not have written).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every table a census writer touches is in the ONE codified set and granted live in dev (recorded via task 145's procedure).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A memo regarding an event whose project is secure is secure-team-owned; `sprk_memo` is in the CHILD taxonomy on both sides and the parity test is green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: when the server refuses (task 146 refusal), option A creates nothing and the UI shows the server's message; option B surfaces the failure and the row is corrected (and reported) by the next job run; no path leaves a secure-parent child user-owned without it appearing in the job report.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: children of non-secure parents keep today's ownership behaviour; an unfiled document save still succeeds unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AUTHORIZATION: every new BFF route is delegated-auth, authorizes the caller against the PARENT record, is listed as gated in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests, and a caller without access to the parent gets the same response as for a non-existent parent.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The reconciliation job runs on a schedule with writes enabled in the deployed configuration template; its watermark pass corrects a user-owned child created under a secure parent outside the product (integration test) and reports what it changed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev): the step-8 sequence is recorded — each client writer and both re-parent paths on all three secure root types (owner read-back, child shares, non-sharee denied), and an OOB MDA quick-create corrected by the job within the recorded interval; probes deleted and the deletion recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF unit/integration/ArchTests green; each changed client package builds with `npm run build:prod` and its jest suite passes; PCF versions bumped in all four locations; publish size reported per CLAUDE.md §10 and ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
